// agentgateway-native: flag a result from a superseded fee-schedule year (mcpGuardrails, response phase)
//
// Matches when the result's `year` is earlier than the calendar year of the
// request (request.startTime). A fee schedule is valid for its whole year, so
// CY2026 data is current all through 2026 and becomes superseded in 2027.
//
// Why not a linear-decay "currency < 0.6" rule here: tested against the real
// rci-knowledge server, an age-from-effective-date rule flagged CY2026 data in
// November as stale (currency 0.15 on a 365-day horizon) although
// list_dataset_snapshots reports it as the current snapshot. Annual fee
// schedules are valid until superseded; they do not decay. Use a decay rule only
// for data that really ages continuously, and EDIT this expression to match how
// your dataset's validity works.
//
// REVIEW-tier: the call is not rejected. The paired
// flag_stale_result.transform.cel adds a `calibration` object to structuredContent.
// Results without a `year` do not match (validity unknown); the completeness
// gate treats a missing year as a missing field.

mcp.tool.name == "lookup_mpfs" &&
has(mcp.result.structuredContent) && "results" in mcp.result.structuredContent &&
size(mcp.result.structuredContent.results) > 0 &&
mcp.result.structuredContent.results[0].with(r,
  "year" in r && r.year != null &&
  int(r.year) < timestamp(request.startTime).getFullYear())
